    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_50286be52ba80330cca5f42f7ce93660dd71df50e797571bf4cb7be558ff6657",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Euler products, Dirichlet series, and divisors are non-equivalent representations of global L-function data. In the convergence region, prime-indexed factors expand into global coefficients; after analytic realization, zeros and poles summarize different global information. The ene-product supplies a proposed algebraic passage in which multiplication of local factor roots corresponds to additive convolution of global divisors, subject to a serious discreteness obstruction.",
