    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_5df5c32485faf1c545fd0cd75352038fb053633075437e8fac1d6acbd09166f7",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The zero-prime explicit formula has an established analytic realization and two more limited comparison representations: contour shifting turns zeros into residues and logarithmic derivatives into prime powers; zero exponentials detect prime-power frequencies through anomalous noncancellation; and the noncommutative-geometric program derives fixed-point and periodic-orbit weights whose transverse determinants have the form required of trace contributions.",
