      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_6b47b7443058726202a9bd595e93a51427a16f884c33b0eb38976fefc6252f9f",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Aspect-specific conductor scales calibrate several comparisons: they order arithmetic families, set the local zero-density scale, and determine the effective matrix-size or logarithmic coordinate in shifted-moment models. In the quadratic moment model, incorporating a gamma-derivative correction into that coordinate removes explicit archimedean dependence from only the first three leading polynomial terms.",
