      "proposed_content": "A truncated reciprocal converts several L-function questions into residual measurements. In a mean square, L times its mollifier measures how much inverse information a chosen length captures; near a zero, the product identity yields alternative large witnesses; and in a separate quadratic family, an engineered initial coefficient gap turns cancellation into off-center mean-square decay.",
