    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_75679dc125ab01834bcab5d63693605ddaa7b68a24a6a7e5a573b5c682431e08",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "A symmetry class may control a leading statistic while arithmetic remains visible in lower-order terms and deterministic centers. In the cited quadratic settings, prime squares create a coherent half-log-log bias, while subtracting the zeta pole in a one-level calculation isolates a universal test-function contribution before the remaining family-dependent terms are analyzed.",
